@* Deliberately NOT the toolkit's default "/profile". Mounting it elsewhere is what exercises
   o.Blazor.ProfilePath in Program.cs — without which the profile-menu item would navigate to /profile and
   404. That was the defect the option was added for, so the sample is where it stays proven. *@
@page "/account"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization

<PageTitle>Profile</PageTitle>

@* The access card (demo mode + "view as") is rendered by UserProfileView between the profile details and
   Claims — see its ShowAccessCard parameter. The way *out* of a reduced session is the banner half of
   <AccessSimulationBar /> in NavMenu, which shows on every page. *@
<UserProfileView />
